That's a useful idea to carve out dedicated time for study. Since a schedule block can't cross midnight, I've split your request into two parts: one block for Friday night and another for early Saturday morning. This will also create a new 'Late Study' goal for you to track your progress.

Here's the proposal:

```coach-proposal
{
  "summary": "Create 'Late Study' goal and add blocks for Friday 11 PM to Saturday 1 AM",
  "actions": [
    {
      "type": "CREATE_GOAL",
      "payload": {
        "title": "Late Study",
        "category": "LEARNING",
        "targetHours": 2,
        "description": "Dedicated time for late-night study to grow as an engineer.",
        "deadline": "2027-02-06"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "CREATE_SCHEDULE_BLOCK",
      "payload": {
        "title": "Late Study",
        "startTime": "23:00",
        "endTime": "23:59",
        "dayOfWeek": 5,
        "category": "LEARNING",
        "goalId": "$ref:0"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "CREATE_SCHEDULE_BLOCK",
      "payload": {
        "title": "Late Study",
        "startTime": "00:00",
        "endTime": "01:00",
        "dayOfWeek": 6,
        "category": "LEARNING",
        "goalId": "$ref:0"
      }
    }
  ]
}
```

This proposal first creates the 'Late Study' goal, then adds a block for Friday from 11:00 PM to 11:59 PM, and another for Saturday from 12:00 AM to 1:00 AM, both linked to the new goal.

You've set a sleep target of 7 hours, aiming for a 10:00 PM bedtime and 4:00 AM wake time. How do you feel this late study block might impact your sleep quality or consistency, especially on Friday night?

I also noticed that many of your existing schedule blocks, like "Morning Prayer", "Family Time", and "Work", aren't currently linked to any goals. Would you like me to help you create goals for these and link your blocks so you can track your time towards them?
